WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.629
-[objects clatter]
-[aswang 2] Hey!

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:07.799
The only way you can get in--
[groans, thuds]

00:00:07.882 --> 00:00:11.302
Greetings, Ibwa, Chief of the Sapa Clan.

00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:13.013
I am Alexandra Trese.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.186
[footsteps]

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:23.523
Good evening, Captain Guerrero.

00:00:23.606 --> 00:00:27.318
Hello, Alexandra. Thanks for coming down.

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:29.988
I had a feeling
you might want to see this.

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:33.158
I admit, I was curious
when you described the circumstances.

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:35.326
So, is it…

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.620
[Alexandra]
The White Lady of Balete Drive.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.956
Any witnesses, Lt. Tapia?

00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:40.999
[Tapia] No, ma'am.

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:45.879
But one of the neighbors positively
ID'd the victim as "Gina Santos."

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:48.548
[Tapia] We checked it, and it turns out
she committed suicide in…

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:50.633
-[paper rustles]
-"…1995."

00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:52.886
Wait, that can't be right.

00:00:53.636 --> 00:00:55.180
Ancient runes crudely done.

00:00:55.305 --> 00:00:57.348
-[Alexandra] Clearly ritual sacrifice.
-[scrapes]

00:00:58.808 --> 00:01:01.853
The bigger question is,
who would want to kill a ghost and why?

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.440
Cover me.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.026
[gunshots]

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:09.694
[growling]

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.159
[slashes]

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:20.121
-[grunting]
-[flesh pierces]

00:01:21.998 --> 00:01:24.292
[yelling]

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.670
[both grunting]

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:30.715
[grunts]

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:32.425
-[slashes]
-[groans]

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:34.052
[flesh rips]

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.265
[hair rustles]

00:01:42.727 --> 00:01:46.022
[tense music]

00:01:50.485 --> 00:01:53.488
[cloth rustles]

00:01:58.493 --> 00:02:00.995
[tense music continues]

00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:07.377
-[line dialing]
-[fire roars]

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.629
[growls]

00:02:09.712 --> 00:02:12.257
Good evening, little Trese.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.592
What game shall we play today?

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.886
Greetings, Great Santelmo.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.429
I'm afraid this is business,

00:02:18.513 --> 00:02:20.765
and I need your help
to uncover what happened.

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:22.851
Well, you're no fun.

00:02:27.021 --> 00:02:30.608
The souls who were killed
in this car are here,

00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:34.154
yet, they are not, and they are not alone.

00:02:36.447 --> 00:02:39.367
I sense spirits on fire.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.579
[Santelmo] People who had burned
to death in their sleep.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.915
They, too, are making the journey.

00:02:46.541 --> 00:02:49.502
How can the souls be here
and yet not be here?

00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:53.173
We are standing in two trains right now.

00:02:53.256 --> 00:02:55.216
[Santelmo] One for the living…

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.010
And the other for the dead.

00:02:57.093 --> 00:03:00.180
Thank you, Santelmo.
May the great light shone upon you.

00:03:00.263 --> 00:03:01.431
[fire roars]

